 "notes": [
  "REFRESH 28 Sep 2026: Sandbanks Brasserie (permanently closed, confirmed via Courier) and Panmure Hotel Monifieth (closed 2018, now apartments, confirmed via Courier) removed from file. Added MAC Cafe (Monifieth Activity Centre) as a new venue.",
  "The Tayberry is NOT in Broughty Ferry any more: left 594 Brook St in 2023 (previously Sandbanks Brasserie, now closed) and relocated to 11 Tay Square, Dundee city centre - belongs to the city-centre remit. thetayberry.co.uk homepage now serves an unrelated adult/spam site (the /menu/ page still shows old Tayberry text) - do not use.",
  "Sol y Sombra (27 Gray St) replaced by Velvet Tide, opened 28 Jun 2026; solysombratapasbar.co.uk still live but stale. Velvet Tide now has its own website (velvet-tide.com) with a menu page, though the menu page loads its dish list via JS so only the category label was captured, not individual dishes.",
  "Forgan's Broughty Ferry: site now readable via TinyFish (still 403 to plain WebFetch). Full menu PDFs, autumn offers and a combined 2026 festive brochure PDF (covering festive dining, Christmas Day and Hogmanay menus at different pages) found; trading upgraded to confirmed.",
  "Collinsons: site now readable via TinyFish (still 403 to plain WebFetch). Site nav now lists 'Lunch Autumn 2026' (cat_id=71) and 'Dinner Autumn 2026' (cat_id=102) as current seasonal menus; cat_id=53 ('Dinner Menu') still serves stale ~2013-era content despite being linked from the homepage; cat_id=66 ('Mid Week Menu') now shows festive-style dishes (roast turkey, Christmas pudding) under its old title/URL - unclear if this is their actual 2026 Christmas menu or stale content. No dedicated Christmas 2026 menu page found via search.",
  "Royal Arch menu PDF (uploaded Dec 2025) still returns 403 to fetcher; link seen on the-royal-arch.com homepage. Full site is JS-rendered so festive/notice content could not be checked this refresh.",
  "The Culdee: site now readable via TinyFish (still 403 to plain WebFetch). Found newer Sep 2025 menu PDFs (food/drinks/kids) that supersede the previously-recorded Nov 2024 food menu PDF; both are still linked from the site.",
  "Milton Inn: site redesigned (new page URLs /food-menu, /festive-menu) but the underlying PDF/PNG menu files are unchanged from last refresh. Festive menu is still a PNG without a year stated - signal left false until year confirmed.",
  "Indos PDF filename dates from ~2019 (V10) - likely old; page unchanged this refresh.",
  "Landmark Hotel (Invergowrie): restaurant.landmarkdundee.co.uk is still JS-only with no readable menu. A separate/newer-looking domain thelandmarkdundee.co.uk/the-landmark-hotel/food-drink/ was found via search but failed with a certificate error (self-signed cert) on both WebFetch and TinyFish - could not verify. Trading left unclear.",
  "New: Monifieth Farm Hotel & Restaurant (Ethiebeaton Park, Arbroath Rd, Monifieth DD5 4HB) opened Aug 2025 as an American roadhouse-style restaurant, but a guest review from Aug 2026 states the restaurant is 'closed for good now' (hotel itself still trading) - not added, evidence conflicting/recent.",
  "1876 Dundee (Queen Street, Broughty Ferry, former Gulistan House) - opened Jun 2025, social inactive since 31 Dec, building now advertised to let (Mar 2026 Courier article) - likely closed but not certain; not added, was not previously in file.",
  "Not found / not verified: Newtown Bar, Barnacles, BrewDog Broughty Ferry (no evidence these exist in remit), Dalhousie Golf Club (Carnoustie, outside remit).",
  "Skipped as takeaway/delivery only: Grill House Monifieth, Meze Grill (Erskine Lane), Seaside Kitchen.",
  "Gaps (no own website or not checked; search budget exhausted): The Fort Bar, Eagle Inn, Post Office Bar, Mali Thai, Gulistan, Gracie's (Facebook only), Raj Mahal Monifieth, The Crown Inn & The Vault Monifieth, The Bay Diner Monifieth, Longparke Farm cafe (site 403), DD4 venues (e.g. The Clep Bar) - none researched to menu level.",
  "The Anchor: food-drinks page was 403 to plain WebFetch; readable via TinyFish which surfaced an actual menu PDF (Mar 2026 upload) not previously recorded.",
  "Goa (Broughty Ferry): /menu page blocked by robots.txt; homepage gives no menu link, kept as-is (no menus).",
  "Second pass 2026-09-28: restaurant.landmarkdundee.co.uk now renders for TinyFish - Dinner, Bar, Kids and Drinks menu PDFs linked from its menu section added; hours listed (breakfast, lunch 12-3, dinner 5:30-8:30) so trading set to confirmed.",
  "Second pass 2026-09-28: Bowmans Monifieth matched to FHRSID 439819 and MAC Cafe to 1775928 (Cafe @ The MAC, Pass 2026-09-10). Velvet Tide: Tripadvisor reviews for 'the new Velvet tide' are posted on the old Sol y Sombra listing (d2046683, 27 Gray Street) - not adopted as its listing.",
  "Refresh 2026-10-05: All 24 venues re-checked (WebFetch + TinyFish). Changes: Bruach festive 2026 menu now a direct PDF (\"XMAS 2026\"); Collinsons stale cat_id=53/66 pages dropped (no longer linked; only Autumn 2026 lunch/dinner linked); new notices for Culdee (Christmas Sessions 19 Dec), Velvet Tide (Chef's Table 5 Dec + events), Forbes weekly deals, Forgan's festive set-menu prices (expired 25 Sep fizz offer removed), Fisherman's Tavern festive dates. No venues dropped or added. Unchanged: Ship Inn (Christmas 2026 menu still live), Jolly's, Royal Arch (still \"coming soon\" site, 2025 PDF), Anchor, Visocchi's (now branded Viso Gelato, 40 Gray St), Indos, Urban Beach, Bowmans x2, Braw Tea, Maison Dieu (food menu still \"coming very soon\"), Milton Inn (festive PNG still undated), MAC Cafe, Invergowrie Inn (no menu PDFs on food page), Forbes, Landmark.",
  "Refresh 2026-10-05: Landmark restaurant site menu section now also lists Morning Tea (10am-12pm) and Afternoon Tea (12-3pm) menus but no linkable URLs were exposed - not added. Goa homepage now describes itself as curry takeaway/order online (no menu link). Velvet Tide menu page still loads dishes via JS.",
  "Refresh 2026-10-05: new-opening searches - The Ferry Selkie (Broughty Ferry, Scottish/Spanish, FHRS 1608554, reviewed by Courier 2023) is an existing venue not in file: no own website found (OpenTable/Tripadvisor only) - gap, not added. Courier headline \"Monifieth A92 restaurant lined up as new Angus Housing Association HQ\" (thecourier.co.uk/fp/news/5448024) further suggests Monifieth Farm restaurant has closed (not in file). Courier \"new cafe opens in Broughty Ferry\" (5287393) and Le Monde/1876 (former Gulistan House) articles were bot-blocked and unverified.",
  "Refresh 2026-10-12: all 24 venues re-checked (WebFetch; TinyFish for Collinsons, Anchor, Forgan's, Culdee, Royal Arch, Velvet Tide, Invergowrie Inn, Landmark). Changes: Forbes of Kingennie 2026 festive brochure PDF replaced by new file (bovkzozkuq.pdf) linked from /christmas-2026; Visocchi's/Viso Gelato closed 8-15 Oct 2026 for refurb (notice added); signal cleared on older items (Anchor Mar 2026 menu, Velvet Tide menu, Culdee Sep 2025 menu). All other menu links unchanged and still linked. Royal Arch still 'coming soon' site with 2025 PDF; Maison Dieu food menu still 'coming very soon'; Milton Inn festive PNG still undated; Goa still takeaway-only, no menu link; Culdee closure 3 Oct (past) not recorded. Ship Inn festive page heading now confirms 'FESTIVE MENU 2026'.",
  "Refresh 2026-10-12: added Mitchell's Broughty Ferry (234 Brook St, DD5 2AH; Scotsman Group cafe/brunch, existing venue missing from file). Its menu page tags lunch and food menus as 'new menu' (no launch date given) - signal left false. New-opening searches (Broughty Ferry, Monifieth) found nothing verifiable with an own website; Sixth Sense Delicatessen (Monikie, opened ~Aug 2026, Facebook only) and Good Day Kitchen & Cafe (Instagram only) noted as unverified gaps.",
  "Second pass 2026-10-12 (late morning): Bruach reopening notice added (menu PDFs on /food unchanged). New Broughty Ferry coffee shop Next Door (339 Brook St, opened 10 Oct 2026) not added - drinks-led, Instagram only, no food menu on own site. Coffee & Co (Dundee city centre) up for sale - not in file."
 ]
}